{"title":"2011 USAJMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find, with proof, all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246268576240cccb709b937e59f7807203de5305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n + 12^n + 2011^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a5003a9ab9c96eee4a9cd7074134b14b1bfb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + (a + b + c)^2 \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"19\" />.  Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9f681c05bd7b174a3441b949d98b47dad707070.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ab + 1}{(a + b)^2} + \\frac{bc + 1}{(b + c)^2} + \\frac{ca + 1}{(c + a)^2} \\ge 3.\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c281449093661a58997ec0451b5de3e644e3438b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = (a,a^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"19\" /> in the coordinate plane, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31abffa9d65dbe91db76ecad89e9b883f024a9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denote the line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.  Consider the set of triangles with vertices of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a4073a555d2c22f2174b59f8e72eed714df0e661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = (a_1, a_1^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c90e1112c3d907cf62fc964b4693206c5f82ffb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 = (a_2, a_2^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d077a46abfde4fca60d62eccf922e8e1df312a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3 = (a_3, a_3^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"19\" />, such that the intersections of the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9bd3da2be6abbbd9dccefd19010d347f8b31921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell(P_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192a1d0a31d92d7dfd50d000b18a52efae148d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell(P_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/0911a8f253cd2a5ba1835446eec649a0d66540d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell(P_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> form an equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.  Find the locus of the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fdeff84fbb19b5242c39fffe43cad6923be0398e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 P_2 P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> ranges over all such triangles.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A <i>word</i> is defined as any finite string of letters.  A word is a <i>palindrome</i> if it reads the same backwards as forwards.  Let a sequence of words <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01c7c994cb63336e404450dcdd76fe9c9d8055a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08ae12b69f1364e6f0aa693d2a051b17383ea82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6a61c0adf995408d4c70c51d35f9798bc472c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" /> be defined as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ef6fdf3ba995a7253ea81d7aca815a316b1499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_0 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c63433719a2526838865f8bcb45cac041bb0c0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_1 = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914a063e8217da4b4f4de459bf82a535c4e81a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is the word formed by writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/062a1894a918fd48805e0f09140bebfea0099f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_{n - 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> followed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d84ee188065ad39272e0da027319c60b15937c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_{n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />.  Prove that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, the word formed by writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08ae12b69f1364e6f0aa693d2a051b17383ea82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6a61c0adf995408d4c70c51d35f9798bc472c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914a063e8217da4b4f4de459bf82a535c4e81a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in succession is a palindrome.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies outside the circle.  The given points are such that (i) lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d6394023b7f71962bce796b61343dcc276679c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> are tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, (ii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear, and (iii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/3290ba498e05f3b7a63b27b064ae74160bc7b526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE} \\parallel \\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the assertion that for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, the remainder upon dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c3455b8d6564924f33e1e4ce8b64d2dd90408c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654a7c7010145200d9d8723eda7ce20e98b5723c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is a power of 4.  Either prove the assertion or find (with proof) a counterexample.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\">USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO\" title=\"2011 USAJMO\">2011 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2010 USAJMO Problems\">2010 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems\">2012 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055031\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 331/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 84/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9477/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   26.188      1 -total\n 78.50%   20.558      1 Template:USAJMO_box\n 19.99%    5.234      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9284:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055031 and revision id 277819. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}